    "body": "Plan (reading research, no branch or PR):\n1. Find DHS/CISA's primary notices on the HIFLD Open shutdown (date, reason, where users were pointed) and an archived copy of the HIFLD Open catalog for the former layer list.\n2. Compare the HIFLD Next catalog against that list: how many layers preserved, how current.\n3. Check source-agency portals for the most-used groups (energy, transportation, emergency services, schools, hospitals, water) for maintained versions and latest data dates.\n4. List layers from licensed/restricted data that are now only in HIFLD Secure or nowhere.\n5. Look for the strongest case against: Living Atlas, data.gov, academic or community archives, or other guides that already answer this.\nParallel subagents for for/against; then rewrite Evidence for/against and Verdict on the card, add Finds, and report here.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
