    "updated_at": "2026-10-18T17:38:14Z",
    "body": "**Verdict:** The three groups hold, but the card's \"nobody has said in one place\" claim is false as stated. DHS's own August 2025 crosswalk already sorted all 305 HIFLD Open layers (51 moved to HIFLD Secure, 254 deprecated with an agency URL), and nearly every layer has a frozen public copy: HIFLD Next has about 299 of 305, and PASDA, DataLumos and SeerAI hold copies too. What's missing is a current, checked version. As of today all 72 HIFLD-hosted links are dead, the 15 EIA layers DHS pointed to now need a login, and 45 of the 51 Secure-only layers (hospitals, schools, law enforcement, power plants, transmission lines) got no public pointer, though several have newer agency substitutes. The article holds if it's framed as \"the official map of where HIFLD went is out of date; here's the checked one.\"\n\n**Numbers.** These come from our own run on 2026-10-18. We parsed the crosswalk, pulled the HIFLD Next catalog from its API and STAC endpoints, and sent an anonymous request to every crosswalk REST URL.\n- **Crosswalk REST links:** 205 of 305 answer. 72 are dead, every one of them hosted by HIFLD. 18 return `Token Required` (15 EIA, 2 DOT, 1 NOAA). 10 failed or timed out.\n- **HIFLD Next coverage:** all 72 dead layers and 17 of the 18 gated ones have a HIFLD Next copy.\n- **HIFLD Next size:** the live stats endpoint reports 330 datasets (525 files). The homepage says 400+, so the draft should say \"400-plus layers in 330 datasets\".\n- **Currency:** 524 of the 525 files are the August 2025 snapshot. Hospitals v1.1.0 is the only update. Some layers are very stale inside: Local Law Enforcement has a SOURCEDATE of 2008\u201309 on nearly every record.\n\n**Main sources** (all added to Finds and related to the card):\n- **Primary:**\n  - DHS crosswalk (DataLumos DOI 10.3886/E241367V1)\n  - DHS HIFLD Open notice page (Wayback, 2025-08-26)\n  - FGDC HIFLD Subcommittee page\n  - EIA Energy Atlas services (our token check)\n  - BTS NTAD, USGS National Structures, NCES EDGE\n- **Secondary:**\n  - NAPSG notice (2025-06-24) and transition webinar (2025-09-25)\n  - PASDA HIFLD_FEMA (214-layer live service)\n  - Data Rescue Project / DataLumos (415 layers)\n  - My Community Data audit\n  - OSM forum thread on substations\n\n**What failed or is unresolved:**\n- No DHS text gives a reason beyond the crosswalk's \"No longer supported as part of the HIFLD mission\". \"No longer a priority\" is a blogger's paraphrase.\n- The \"March 2025\" announcement date in our NGAC slides is unconfirmed. The earliest dated notice we found is 24 June 2025.\n- DHS 2026 User Forum videos mention a \"HIFLD Shared\" tier. We couldn't define it; check it before the draft.\n- The layer matching is by title, with near-misses reviewed by hand. We didn't compare layer contents.\n\nReady for review\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
